ith Coquimbo Unido introducing veteran presence in Lucas Pratto , while Tolima looked for fresh legs in the final third. Jersson Gonzalez Decides the Contest The managerial gamble from the Deportes Tolima dugout proved to be the masterstroke of the evening. In the 70th minute, Jersson Gonzalez was introduced to the fray, and it took him only eight minutes to make a defining impact on the match. In the 78th minute, Gonzalez found space in the box and fired home to put the hosts back in front, sparking wild celebrations in the stands. As the clock ticked toward the final whistle, Coquimbo Unido pushed for a second equalizer, but their frustrations grew as Guido Vadala was cautioned in the 84th minute. Tolima managed the closing stages with composure, navigating six minutes of stoppage time to secure all three points. The referee’s final whistle confirmed a hard-fought victory for the Colombian side, leaving the visitors to rue their missed opportunities in a pulsating second half."
